// Jina Search REST (s.jina.ai): the `jina` provider of the web_search chain.
//
// Search only. Jina Reader (r.jina.ai), which fetches and converts one page,
// is not declared: page reading is out of scope for web_search.
//
// Wire contract pinned from Jina's own documentation (read 2026-10-20):
// - the search operation of Jina's published OpenAPI document,
//   https://s.jina.ai/openapi.json (path /{q}, its parameters, headers and
//   listed responses);
// - the Search API guide, https://docs.jina.ai/reader-api (Authorization,
//   X-Site and X-Respond-With headers);
// - the Search section and rate-limit table of the Reader page,
//   https://jina.ai/reader/#search and https://jina.ai/reader/#rate-limit;
// - the README and search source of Jina's open-source server,
//   https://github.com/jina-ai/reader (README.md, src/api/searcher.ts,
//   src/services/serp/serper.ts), where the documents are silent.
//
// - method and path: GET https://s.jina.ai/<url-encoded query>, the OpenAPI
//   path /{q} and the README's form. The query is sent as that whole path
//   segment, fully percent-encoded (the manifest marks `q` a free-text path
//   parameter, so a "/" in a query is sent as %2F rather than refused, and
//   diagnostics print "/{q}", never the query). Jina also documents a ?q=
//   form (Reader page) and POST with a JSON body (Search API guide); neither
//   is used;
// - auth: "Authorization: Bearer <key>" (guide and OpenAPI), so the key goes
//   in `Authorization` with the `Bearer ` prefix. The rate-limit table marks
//   keyless search blocked. The connection is bound to the vault credential
//   `apikey:jina`; plexus reads it by name at dispatch and never stores it;
// - request fields used: `count` (query parameter; the OpenAPI and server
//   source accept 0 to 20, default 10; 1 to 20 is sent), and one domain in
//   the `X-Site` header (guide). JSON output comes from
//   `Accept: application/json`, which the REST transport sends on every
//   request. `X-Respond-With: no-content` is sent on every request as a
//   reviewed constant: the guide says it leaves page content out, and the
//   server source then returns the search listings without fetching each
//   result page, which web_search never reads. The OpenAPI also documents
//   `num` (an alias of count), `site` as a query parameter, gl, hl, location,
//   page, provider and crawler headers; none are sent and they are not in
//   the reviewed schema;
// - reply: {code, status, data, meta}, where `data` is an array of results
//   with `title`, `url`, `description` (the listing snippet) and `content`
//   (empty when no page content is fetched); the server's listings may carry
//   a `date`, and fetched pages a `publishedTime`;
// - errors: the OpenAPI lists 400 ParamValidationError, 401
//   AuthenticationFailedError/AuthenticationRequiredError, 402
//   InsufficientBalanceError, 403 AbuseAlleviationError, 422
//   AssertionFailureError, 429 RateLimitTriggeredError, 500
//   DownstreamServiceError and 503 ServiceBadAttemptError, as JSON bodies.
//   No Retry-After header is documented;
// - limits: no query-length limit is documented (the OpenAPI `q` has no
//   maxLength); the rate-limit table gives s.jina.ai 100 requests per minute
//   for free and paid keys and 1,000 for premium keys.
//
// Differences from the provider facts the web_search chain design started from
// (GET https://s.jina.ai/<url-encoded query>; Bearer auth; count, max 20;
// one domain via X-Site; title, url, description or content):
// - none in method, path, auth, count or the result fields named there;
// - X-Site is in the Search API guide but not in the OpenAPI document, which
//   lists a `site` query parameter instead. The README and server source
//   also accept several sites (repeated `site` parameters, or a list split on
//   ", " in the header); the design allows one domain, so the backend
//   declares a maximum of one and two or more domains skip Jina;
// - X-Respond-With: no-content is sent in addition. If Jina ignored it, the
//   reply would only carry extra `content`, and `description` would still be
//   read first;
// - recency: Jina documents no date filter, so a search with recency skips
//   Jina for capability instead of returning results of any age;
// - query length: none is documented, so the tool's own 500-character limit
//   applies;
// - a publication date is reported from `date` or `publishedTime` when it is
//   a parseable date, and dropped otherwise;
// - empty results: the official OpenAPI (https://s.jina.ai/openapi.json,
//   read 2026-10-20) documents 422 AssertionFailureError for a mismatch of
//   X-Assert-Status-Code, not as a stable no-results code. Plexus declares no
//   such request header and its reviewed schema cannot supply it. A 422 is
//   therefore unexpected and still stops as a rejected request; no no_results
//   signal is declared. A 200 with empty `data` is served as an empty result;
// - classification needs no Jina-specific rule: 401 is a credential failure,
//   402 a quota skip with the one-hour cooldown, 429 throttled for 60
//   seconds (or a Retry-After, if one is ever sent), 403 another client error
//   and 500 and 503 server errors, all three unavailable for 60 seconds.
//
// The search action is read-risk and has no side effects, so a retry is safe.
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "key": "jina_rest",
  "name": "Jina Search (REST)",
  "description": "Web search over Jina's Search API (s.jina.ai), as a provider for web_search.",
  "reuse_path": "openapi_shim",
  "reuse_rationale": "Documented REST API with a published OpenAPI spec and static API-key bearer auth; a search mutates no vendor-side state, so it maps to a read grant.",
  "tier": "S1",
  "transport": {
    "kind": "rest_api",
    "url": "https://s.jina.ai"
  },
  "auth": {
    "mode": "api_key"
  },
  "credential_bindings": [
    {
      "ref_role": "api_key",
      "placement": "header",
      "key": "Authorization",
      "prefix": "Bearer ",
      "required": true
    }
  ],
  "resource_filters": {
    "required": [],
    "optional": [],
    "write_enabling": []
  },
  "actions_baseline": [
    {
      "name": "search",
      "risk": "read",
      "http": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/{q}",
        "parameters": "query",
        "text_path_parameters": ["q"],
        "header_parameters": {
          "site": "X-Site",
          "respond_with": "X-Respond-With"
        },
        "request_constants": {
          "respond_with": "no-content"
        },
        "args_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "q": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 500 },
            "count": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 20 },
            "site": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 253 }
          },
          "required": ["q"],
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "ask_first_risk": ["write", "destructive"],
    "rate_limit": { "calls_per_min": 30 }
  },
  "availability": "ga"
}
